# the voicing (CHORDS' Height and Spread, every way to play chords): Height is the top note, the chord tone nearest it;
# the other two hang under it by Spread; a chord change keeps the top near (the voices lead); a Height detent is the
# next chord tone. MIDI notes: C3 48, C5 72.
tapkey 7
wait 300
# C: the top C5 at Height C5, E4 and G4 under it (Spread 12: the middle near A#4, the lowest near C4)
expect top 72
expect note0 48
expect note2 64
expect note1 67
expect note3 72
# Am (the black key F#4 arms minor): its top stays near, A4 or C5; C5 the nearer
tapkey 13
tapkey 4
wait 300
expect top 72
# back to C, Height a detent up: E5, then a detent down: C5 again
tapkey 13
tapkey 7
wait 300
kpage 1
turn K2 1
wait 300
expect top 76
turn K2 -1
wait 300
expect top 72
# Spread 0: close under the top, each the nearest below: G4, then E4
turn K3 -12
wait 300
expect note1 67
expect note2 64
